Peano writes different types of files: Some history data (point probes)
yield plain csv files, particles typically can dump into VTK files 
directly, which you can open with tools such as <a href="https://pyvista.org/">PyVista</a>, Paraview or VisIt.
The majority of volumetric Eulerian data in Peano however is dumped in
a bespoke Peano data file format.
This data format is also used to display "only" meshes or domain decomposition.
 



